### A7: Search in Rotated Sorted Array ⭐⭐⭐⭐
**Difficulty**: Medium | **Companies**: Google, Amazon, Microsoft
```
TRICK: At any mid point, one half is always sorted.
  If arr[left] <= arr[mid]: LEFT half is sorted
    → Check if target is in [arr[left], arr[mid]]
  Else: RIGHT half is sorted
    → Check if target is in [arr[mid], arr[right]]
```
```python
def search(nums, target):
    left, right = 0, len(nums) - 1

    while left <= right:
        mid = (left + right) // 2

        if nums[mid] == target:
            return mid

        if nums[left] <= nums[mid]:     # Left half is sorted
            if nums[left] <= target < nums[mid]:
                right = mid - 1
            else:
                left = mid + 1
        else:                           # Right half is sorted
            if nums[mid] < target <= nums[right]:
                left = mid + 1
            else:
                right = mid - 1

    return -1

# Time: O(log n) | Space: O(1)
```

