### S4: Longest Palindromic Substring ⭐⭐⭐⭐
**Difficulty**: Medium | **Companies**: Amazon, Google
```
APPROACH — Expand from Center:
  A palindrome mirrors around its center.
  For each character (and each gap between chars), expand outward.
  Odd length: center = single char
  Even length: center = gap between two equal chars
```
```python
def longestPalindrome(s):
    result = ""

    def expand(left, right):
        while left >= 0 and right < len(s) and s[left] == s[right]:
            left -= 1
            right += 1
        return s[left + 1:right]        # Slice AFTER loop (went one too far)

    for i in range(len(s)):
        odd = expand(i, i)              # Odd-length palindrome
        even = expand(i, i + 1)         # Even-length palindrome

        if len(odd) > len(result):
            result = odd
        if len(even) > len(result):
            result = even

    return result

# Time: O(n²) | Space: O(1)
```

