## Common Mistakes & Fixes

### Array Problems
```
❌ Forgetting boundary checks (index out of range)
✅ Always check: i < len(arr), i >= 0

❌ Not handling empty input
✅ Add: if not arr: return default_value

❌ Off-by-one errors
✅ Use range(len(arr)-1) vs range(len(arr))

❌ Modifying while iterating
✅ Either iterate backwards or collect indices first
```

### String Problems
```
❌ Treating strings as mutable
✅ Convert to list/array or use proper methods

❌ Not considering edge cases (single char, empty)
✅ Add explicit checks at start

❌ Incorrect substring extraction
✅ Remember: s[i:j] doesn't include s[j]
```

### Linked List Problems
```
❌ Not handling null/None properly
✅ Check: if not node or if node is None

❌ Creating cycles accidentally
✅ Be careful with node.next assignments

❌ Not using dummy node for operations
✅ Use dummy = ListNode(0); dummy.next = head
```

### Tree Problems
```
❌ Forgetting recursion base case
✅ Always have: if not node: return ...

❌ Modifying tree structure unintentionally
✅ Create new nodes if needed

❌ Not handling null paths
✅ Check both left and right are valid
```

### Graph Problems
```
❌ Forgetting to mark visited nodes
✅ Mark visited immediately when discovered

❌ Not handling disconnected components
✅ Loop through all nodes, not just from start

❌ Infinite loops in cycles
✅ Always mark nodes as visited
```

