## Common Mistakes in Interviews

### Code Mistakes
```
❌ Not initializing variables
❌ Off-by-one errors in loops
❌ Forgetting base cases in recursion
❌ Not checking null/None
❌ Modifying input unintentionally
❌ Integer overflow (not in Python)
```

### Logic Mistakes
```
❌ Wrong algorithm choice
❌ Incorrect complexity analysis
❌ Missing edge cases
❌ Not handling empty input
❌ Greedy when needs DP
```

### Communication Mistakes
```
❌ Coding without explaining
❌ Not asking for clarification
❌ Giving up too quickly
❌ Not discussing trade-offs
❌ Wrong time/space complexity
❌ Not testing your code
```

### Recovery Strategies
```
If you're stuck:
1. Ask the interviewer for a hint
2. Talk through your thinking
3. Start with brute force
4. Use simpler examples
5. Discuss what you'd do if you had more time
```

